11	## 1. `src/components/Graphs/GraphTimeTooltip/GraphTimeTooltip.tsx`
12	
13	```tsx
14	import dayjs from 'dayjs';
15	import { type TooltipProps } from 'recharts';
16	
17	import Typography from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Typography';
18	import TooltipStack from 'components/Graphs/TooltipStack';
19	import {
20		type Duration,
21		tooltipDateFormat,
22	} from 'components/Graphs/graphMeasurements';
23	
24	export interface GraphTimeTooltipProps extends TooltipProps<number, string> {
25		duration: Duration;
26	}
27	
28	/**
29	 * Recharts tooltip content that renders the hovered point's timestamp,
30	 * formatted per the given duration. `active`/`payload` are injected by recharts;
31	 * `duration` is supplied by the consuming chart.
32	 */
33	const GraphTimeTooltip = ({
34		active,
35		payload,
36		duration,
37	}: GraphTimeTooltipProps) => {
38		if (!active || !payload?.length) return null;
39		const time = payload[0]?.payload?.time as number | undefined;
40		if (time == null) return null;
41		return (
42			<TooltipStack>
43				<Typography variant="label-md">
44					{dayjs.unix(time).format(tooltipDateFormat(duration))}
45				</Typography>
46			</TooltipStack>
47		);
48	};
49	
50	export default GraphTimeTooltip;
51	```
52	
53	**Behavior:** This is the `content` renderer passed to recharts' `<Tooltip>`. It receives `active`/`payload` from recharts automatically and a custom `duration` prop from the consuming chart. It renders nothing when inactive or empty. When active, it pulls `time` (a unix timestamp) off the first payload entry's underlying data point and formats it via `dayjs.unix(time).format(...)`, using `tooltipDateFormat(duration)` — `'MMM D, YYYY'` for `'2week'` duration, `'h:mm a'` otherwise. It wraps the label in `TooltipStack`, a styled `Stack`. **This is the entire tooltip — a floating box positioned by recharts' default tooltip positioning logic (no custom position/coordinate prop, no cursor customization, no reference line).**
54	
55	## 2. `src/components/Graphs/TooltipStack/TooltipStack.jsx`
56	
57	```jsx
58	// @ts-check
59	
60	import React from 'react';
61	import Stack from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Stack';
62	import combineSx from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/utility/combineSx';
63	
64	/** @param {import('@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Stack').StackProps} props */
65	const TooltipStack = ({ sx, ...rest }) => {
66		return (
67			<Stack
68				sx={combineSx(
69					{
70						backgroundColor: (theme) => theme.vars.palette.uc.bg.main,
71						borderRadius: (theme) => theme.borderRadius.roundedXS,
72						boxShadow: (theme) => theme.shadows[1],
73						padding: (theme) => `${theme.spacing(50)} ${theme.spacing(100)}`,
74						gap: 50,
75					},
76					sx,
77				)}
78				{...rest}
79			/>
80		);
81	};
82	
83	export default TooltipStack;
84	```
85	
86	**Behavior:** Pure styling wrapper around Undercurrent's `Stack`. Background = theme `uc.bg.main`, border-radius `roundedXS`, `boxShadow[1]` (a drop shadow), padding `spacing(50) spacing(100)` (vertical/horizontal), and internal `gap: 50` between stacked children. This is the visual "pill/card" box behind the tooltip content. It accepts any `Stack` props and merges `sx`.
