Confirmed — every `strokeDasharray` usage in the current-gen "Graphs" module family is only the `CartesianGrid` background grid (`5 5` dashed grid lines), not a hover reference line. There is no `ReferenceLine`, `activeDot`, cursor customization, or any dashed-vertical-line-plus-dot hover indicator anywhere in this codebase. The tooltip is purely the floating `GraphTimeTooltip` box rendered via recharts' default `Tooltip` positioning.

Here is the full report.

## Branch/repo confirmation

Repo: `/Users/trounceabout/Documents/Repos/Work/wallaby`, branch `feature/epic-server-monitoring-dashboard` (already checked out, up to date with origin).

---

## 1. `src/components/Graphs/GraphTimeTooltip/GraphTimeTooltip.tsx`

```tsx
import dayjs from 'dayjs';
import { type TooltipProps } from 'recharts';

import Typography from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Typography';
import TooltipStack from 'components/Graphs/TooltipStack';
import {
	type Duration,
	tooltipDateFormat,
} from 'components/Graphs/graphMeasurements';

export interface GraphTimeTooltipProps extends TooltipProps<number, string> {
	duration: Duration;
}

/**
 * Recharts tooltip content that renders the hovered point's timestamp,
 * formatted per the given duration. `active`/`payload` are injected by recharts;
 * `duration` is supplied by the consuming chart.
 */
const GraphTimeTooltip = ({
	active,
	payload,
	duration,
}: GraphTimeTooltipProps) => {
	if (!active || !payload?.length) return null;
	const time = payload[0]?.payload?.time as number | undefined;
	if (time == null) return null;
	return (
		<TooltipStack>
			<Typography variant="label-md">
				{dayjs.unix(time).format(tooltipDateFormat(duration))}
			</Typography>
		</TooltipStack>
	);
};

export default GraphTimeTooltip;
```

**Behavior:** This is the `content` renderer passed to recharts' `<Tooltip>`. It receives `active`/`payload` from recharts automatically and a custom `duration` prop from the consuming chart. It renders nothing when inactive or empty. When active, it pulls `time` (a unix timestamp) off the first payload entry's underlying data point and formats it via `dayjs.unix(time).format(...)`, using `tooltipDateFormat(duration)` — `'MMM D, YYYY'` for `'2week'` duration, `'h:mm a'` otherwise. It wraps the label in `TooltipStack`, a styled `Stack`. **This is the entire tooltip — a floating box positioned by recharts' default tooltip positioning logic (no custom position/coordinate prop, no cursor customization, no reference line).**

## 2. `src/components/Graphs/TooltipStack/TooltipStack.jsx`

```jsx
// @ts-check

import React from 'react';
import Stack from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Stack';
import combineSx from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/utility/combineSx';

/** @param {import('@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Stack').StackProps} props */
const TooltipStack = ({ sx, ...rest }) => {
	return (
		<Stack
			sx={combineSx(
				{
					backgroundColor: (theme) => theme.vars.palette.uc.bg.main,
					borderRadius: (theme) => theme.borderRadius.roundedXS,
					boxShadow: (theme) => theme.shadows[1],
					padding: (theme) => `${theme.spacing(50)} ${theme.spacing(100)}`,
					gap: 50,
				},
				sx,
			)}
			{...rest}
		/>
	);
};

export default TooltipStack;
```

**Behavior:** Pure styling wrapper around Undercurrent's `Stack`. Background = theme `uc.bg.main`, border-radius `roundedXS`, `boxShadow[1]` (a drop shadow), padding `spacing(50) spacing(100)` (vertical/horizontal), and internal `gap: 50` between stacked children. This is the visual "pill/card" box behind the tooltip content. It accepts any `Stack` props and merges `sx`.

## 3. `src/components/Graphs/StatHighlight/StatHighlight.tsx`

```tsx
import Box, { type BoxProps } from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Box';
import Typography from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Typography';
import TrendingUpIcon from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/icons/lucide/TrendingUp';
import TrendingDownIcon from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/icons/lucide/TrendingDown';
import combineSx from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/utility/combineSx';

export interface StatHighlightProps extends BoxProps {
	/** Monospace label shown above the value, e.g. "1 min". Omit when the card header serves as the label. */
	label?: string;
	/**
	 * Full formatted value string including any short suffix, e.g. "64%", "75%", "3.8".
	 * Do NOT use unit= for %; unit= is for longer secondary values like "14.2/16 GB".
	 */
	value: string;
	/** Optional secondary value shown in the extras column, e.g. "14.2/16 GB". */
	unit?: string;
	/** Optional % change. Positive = up, negative = down. */
	changePercent?: number;
	/**
	 * Optional custom change label rendered instead of "±N%", e.g. "+1.5 GB/day".
	 * When provided, changePercent is not required — use changeDirection to control the icon.
	 */
	changeLabel?: string;
	/**
	 * Explicit icon direction when changeLabel is used without changePercent.
	 * Defaults to 'up' when changePercent >= 0.
	 */
	changeDirection?: 'up' | 'down';
	/**
	 * Color applied to the percent change icon and text. Defaults to text.weak.
	 * Pass a resolved CSS color for semantic meaning, e.g. vars.palette.uc.success.text.main.
	 */
	changeColor?: string;
	/** Optional 12×12 rounded-square color key shown in the label row (Load Average series). */
	iconColor?: string;
	/**
	 * Override color for the large value. Defaults to text.main.
	 * Pass a resolved CSS color, e.g. vars.palette.uc.danger.text.main for critical states.
	 */
	valueColor?: string;
}

/**
 * Stat highlight matching the Figma "Highlight" component spec.
 * Layout: label row → score row (large value + extras column).
 */
const StatHighlight = ({
	label,
	value,
	unit,
	changePercent,
	changeLabel,
	changeDirection,
	changeColor,
	iconColor,
	valueColor,
	sx,
	...rest
}: StatHighlightProps) => {
	const hasChange =
		(changePercent !== undefined && changePercent !== null) ||
		Boolean(changeLabel);
	// changeDirection wins; fall back to sign of changePercent; default to up when neither is set
	const isPositive =
		changeDirection === 'up' ||
		(changeDirection === undefined &&
			(changePercent !== undefined ? changePercent >= 0 : true));
	const hasExtras = Boolean(unit) || hasChange;

	return (
		<Box
			sx={combineSx({ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 100 }, sx)}
			{...rest}
		>
			{/* Label row — only rendered when label or iconColor is provided */}
			{(label || iconColor) && (
				<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', gap: 100 }}>
					{iconColor && (
						<Box
							sx={({ size, borderRadius }) => ({
								width: size.xXS,
								height: size.xXS,
								borderRadius: borderRadius.roundedSm,
								backgroundColor: iconColor,
								flexShrink: 0,
							})}
						/>
					)}
					<Typography
						fontType="monospace"
						variant="label-md"
						sx={({ vars }) => ({ color: vars.palette.uc.text.weak })}
					>
						{label}
					</Typography>
				</Box>
			)}

			{/* Score row */}
			<Box
				sx={{
					display: 'flex',
					alignItems: 'flex-end',
					gap: 100,
					width: '100%',
				}}
			>
				{/* Large value */}
				{/* TODO: hardcoded scale pending a typographic-scale decision; replace with a UC variant before release. */}
				<Typography
					sx={({ vars }) => ({
						fontSize: '40px',
						lineHeight: '38px',
						letterSpacing: '-0.64px',
						color: valueColor ?? vars.palette.uc.text.main,
						whiteSpace: 'nowrap',
					})}
				>
					{value}
				</Typography>

				{/* Extras column — unit + % change stacked */}
				{hasExtras && (
					<Box
						sx={{
							display: 'flex',
							flexDirection: 'column',
							alignItems: 'flex-start',
							justifyContent: 'flex-end',
							gap: 50,
						}}
					>
						{unit && (
							<Typography
								fontType="monospace"
								variant="label-md"
								sx={({ vars }) => ({
									color: vars.palette.uc.text.weak,
									whiteSpace: 'nowrap',
								})}
							>
								{unit}
							</Typography>
						)}

						{hasChange && (
							<Box
								sx={({ vars }) => ({
									display: 'flex',
									alignItems: 'center',
									gap: 50,
									color: changeColor ?? vars.palette.uc.text.weak,
								})}
							>
								{isPositive ? (
									<TrendingUpIcon
										sx={({ size }) => ({ width: size.xS, height: size.xS })}
									/>
								) : (
									<TrendingDownIcon
										sx={({ size }) => ({ width: size.xS, height: size.xS })}
									/>
								)}
								<Typography fontType="monospace" variant="label-md">
									{changeLabel ??
										`${isPositive ? '+' : '-'}${Math.abs(changePercent ?? 0)}%`}
								</Typography>
							</Box>
						)}
					</Box>
				)}
			</Box>
		</Box>
	);
};

export default StatHighlight;
```

**Behavior:** Two-row layout — optional label row (monospace weak-color text + optional 12×12 `roundedSm` color swatch via `iconColor`), then a score row with a large 40px/38px-line-height/-0.64px-letter-spacing value, and an "extras" column stacked to the right containing an optional `unit` (monospace, weak color) and an optional change indicator (Trending Up/Down lucide icon + monospace text, colored via `changeColor`, default `text.weak`). Change text defaults to `±N%` from `changePercent`, or a custom `changeLabel` string (e.g., "+1.5 GB/day", "New"). Direction/icon chosen by `changeDirection` if given, else sign of `changePercent`, defaulting to "up".

## 4. `src/components/Graphs/GraphCard/GraphCard.tsx`

```tsx
import { type ReactNode } from 'react';

import Card, { type CardProps } from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Card';
import CardContent from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/CardContent';
import CardHeader from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/CardHeader';
import CardLayeredFooter from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/CardLayeredFooter';
import IconButton from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/IconButton';
import Tooltip from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/Tooltip';
import InfoIcon from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/icons/lucide/Info';
import combineSx from '@liquidweb-dev/undercurrent/utility/combineSx';

export interface GraphCardInfoTooltip {
	message: string;
	ariaLabel: string;
	arrow?: boolean;
}

export interface GraphCardProps extends CardProps {
	title: string;
	infoTooltip?: GraphCardInfoTooltip;
	/** Optional footer content rendered in a CardLayeredFooter below the body. */
	footer?: ReactNode;
	/** Background color for the footer — pass a theme color for urgency treatment. */
	footerBgcolor?: string;
}

/**
 * Shared card chrome for graph modules: a Card with a titled header (and an
 * optional info tooltip action) wrapping the graph content, plus an optional
 * footer. Extends CardProps so callers can pass through any MUI Card prop and
 * merge their own sx.
 */
const GraphCard = ({
	title,
	infoTooltip,
	footer,
	footerBgcolor,
	sx,
	children,
	...rest
}: GraphCardProps) => (
	<Card
		sx={combineSx(
			{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', overflow: 'hidden' },
			sx,
		)}
		{...rest}
	>
		<CardHeader
			title={title}
			action={
				infoTooltip ? (
					<Tooltip
						arrow={infoTooltip.arrow}
						variant="fancy"
						title=""
						message={infoTooltip.message}
					>
						<IconButton
							variant="barebones"
							size="small"
							aria-label={infoTooltip.ariaLabel}
						>
							<InfoIcon />
						</IconButton>
					</Tooltip>
				) : undefined
			}
		/>
		<CardContent
			sx={{
				display: 'flex',
				flexDirection: 'column',
				flexGrow: 1,
				overflow: 'hidden',
				p: 0,
			}}
		>
			{children}
		</CardContent>
		{footer && (
			<CardLayeredFooter bgcolor={footerBgcolor}>{footer}</CardLayeredFooter>
		)}
	</Card>
);

export default GraphCard;
```

**Behavior:** The shared card chrome for every graph module — `Card` (flex column, `overflow: hidden`) → `CardHeader` (title + optional info-icon button with a "fancy" tooltip) → `CardContent` (flex-grow, `overflow: hidden`, `p: 0`, holds `children`) → optional `CardLayeredFooter` (with `bgcolor` override, used e.g. for danger-red disk-full footer).

## 5. `src/components/Graphs/graphMeasurements.ts`

```ts
import type { Theme } from '@mui/material/styles';
import type { LWApiPublicAssetMeasurementsLookupParamsRawI } from '@liquidweb-dev/club-sauce/public/asset/measurements/index.raw';
import { type StatHighlightProps } from 'components/Graphs/StatHighlight';

/** Measurement lookup duration window (e.g. '12hour', 'day', '2week'). */
export type Duration = LWApiPublicAssetMeasurementsLookupParamsRawI['duration'];

/**
 * Result of a change computation: a rounded percent, `'new'` when the previous
 * period/point was a genuine zero and the current value is positive (a real
 * signal, not a percentage), or undefined when unknown or flat.
 */
export type ChangeResult = number | 'new' | undefined;

/** dayjs format string for tooltip timestamps — date for long windows, time otherwise. */
export const tooltipDateFormat = (duration: Duration) =>
	duration === '2week' ? 'MMM D, YYYY' : 'h:mm a';

/**
 * Maps each display duration to a doubled window so we can fetch the previous
 * period alongside the current one and compute period-over-period change.
 * TODO: the doubled values here (e.g. day -> 3day, month -> 3month) need review;
 * this comparison will ultimately move to the backend API.
 */
export const DOUBLED_DURATION: Partial<Record<Duration, Duration>> = {
	'6hour': '12hour',
	'12hour': 'day',
	day: '3day',
	'2week': 'month',
	month: '3month',
} as const;

/** Mean of `key` across data points that have a value; skips null/missing readings. */
export const avg = (data: Array<Record<string, number>>, key: string) => {
	const present = data.filter((p) => p[key] != null);
	if (!present.length) return 0;
	return present.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p[key], 0) / present.length;
};

/**
 * Point-to-previous-point percentage change for `key` at `index`.
 * Returns undefined for the first point or when either value is missing.
 * Returns 'new' when the previous point was a genuine zero and the current
 * point is positive, rather than hiding the spike as "unknown".
 */
export const computeChange = (
	data: Array<Record<string, number>>,
	key: string,
	index: number,
): ChangeResult => {
	if (index < 1) return undefined;
	const current = data[index][key];
	const previous = data[index - 1][key];
	if (current == null || previous == null) return undefined;
	if (previous === 0) return current > 0 ? 'new' : undefined;
	return Math.round(((current - previous) / previous) * 100);
};

/**
 * Period-over-period percentage change between a current and previous average.
 * See ChangeResult for the 'new'-baseline sentinel.
 */
export const periodChange = (
	currentAvg: number,
	prevAvg: number,
): ChangeResult => {
	if (prevAvg === 0) return currentAvg > 0 ? 'new' : undefined;
	return Math.round(((currentAvg - prevAvg) / prevAvg) * 100);
};

/** Danger for an increase (including 'new'), success for a decrease; undefined when change is flat or unknown. */
export const changeColorForIncrease = (
	changePercent: ChangeResult,
	theme: Theme,
) => {
	if (changePercent === undefined) return undefined;
	if (changePercent === 'new' || changePercent > 0)
		return theme.vars.palette.uc.danger.text.main;
	if (typeof changePercent === 'number' && changePercent < 0)
		return theme.vars.palette.uc.success.text.main;
	return undefined;
};

/** Maps a ChangeResult to the StatHighlight props that render it. */
export const changeResultToStatHighlightProps = (
	change: ChangeResult,
): Pick<
	StatHighlightProps,
	'changePercent' | 'changeLabel' | 'changeDirection'
> => {
	if (change === 'new') return { changeLabel: 'New', changeDirection: 'up' };
	if (change === undefined) return {};
	return { changePercent: change };
};
```

**Behavior:** Shared math/formatting utilities. `tooltipDateFormat` — the key detail: `'2week'` duration → `'MMM D, YYYY'` (e.g. "May 9, 2026"); every other duration → `'h:mm a'` (e.g. "2:30 pm"). `DOUBLED_DURATION` maps a display window to a "fetch double, split at midpoint" window used by all the charts to compute period-over-period change. `avg`, `computeChange` (point-to-previous-point %), `periodChange` (avg-vs-avg %), `changeColorForIncrease` (danger red if increase/new, success green if decrease), and `changeResultToStatHighlightProps` (adapts a `ChangeResult` into `StatHighlight` props, turning `'new'` into a `changeLabel: 'New'`).

