I now have everything needed. Here is the complete implementation plan.

---

# Implementation Plan: Watchtower "Live Modules" Dashboard

## 0. Container width (confirmed from `ProjectLayout.astro`)

Chain: `<main class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] py-18">` → `<article class="px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-[60px]">` → `.article-body` (no additional max-width/padding of its own — comment at line 245 confirms `.article-body` inherits `<article>`'s horizontal margin). At `lg` (≥1024px) and up to 1120px viewport, effective content width is **1120 − 2×60 = 1000px max**, shrinking as viewport narrows below 1120px (article stays `mx-auto` full-bleed inside main until main's own max-width caps it). Below `sm` (640px), padding drops to `px-6` (24px/side). This confirms the Figma's ~1000px design width is in fact close to the actual max container width, so the grid should be built fluid (`fr` tracks, `gap`, `min-width: 0` on grid items) rather than fixed-px, and should look correct at exactly ~1000px while also degrading gracefully from ~320px up.

## 1. Dependency

```
bun add recharts
```

Confirmed: recharts `3.9.2` lists `react ^19.0.0` in `peerDependencies` — compatible with this repo's React 19.2.4. No other new dependency needed. For the "May 9, 2026" date format, use native `Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" })` (or equivalent `toLocaleDateString`) — no dayjs required, matching the repo's existing zero-date-library footprint.

