**Mock data placement**: single shared `mockData.ts`, not per-component `__mockData__` folders like Wallaby. Rationale: Wallaby's per-component mock folders exist because that repo has many independent chart consumers across different features/pages; here all 5 mock series are consumed by exactly one sandbox for one case study, need to share a consistent time axis (so hovering conceptually "lines up" across cards, even though each card manages hover state independently), and keeping them in one file makes it trivial to eyeball-tune the whole dashboard's numbers together. If this grows, splitting later is cheap.

**Why `WtCard` instead of reusing `UcCard`**: `UcCard.tsx` bakes one fixed layout (title → headline+trend → stats row → footer note) directly into a single non-composable component, by its own doc comment's admission ("nothing else on the site needs a reusable Card"). Wallaby's `GraphCard` needs a composable header/content/footer split (chart cards have no footer; Disk space has a colored footer bar; content varies per card: chart vs. MeasureBar vs. StatHighlight row). `WtCard` should expose `title`, optional `infoTooltip`/icon flag, `children` (content), and an optional `footer` slot that accepts its own background-color override (for Disk space's red bar) — this needs actual composability that `UcCard` doesn't offer, hence a new component family per the requirements.

